# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages _redirects syntax.
#
# This rebuild did not move any previously-indexable URL path. The old site
# was a single index.html at "/" with in-page fragment anchors
# (#core-lanes, #product-lanes, #about, #network, #top). Fragments are never
# sent to the server, so they can't be handled here — instead, the new
# home page (src/pages/index.astro) keeps the same element ids
# (#core-lanes, #product-lanes, #about, #network, #top) so any bookmarked
# "https://texasmovement.com/#core-lanes"-style link still lands on
# equivalent content. See docs/MIGRATION_INVENTORY.md for the full
# before/after content map.
#
# No path-level redirects are needed for this release. Add entries here in
# the form `/<old-path> /<new-path> 301` if a future restructuring moves a
# real, indexed path.

# Apex domain (texasmovement.com) is canonical. www.texasmovement.com redirects
# permanently here. This rule only takes effect once www.texasmovement.com is also
# added as a custom domain on the same Cloudflare Pages project — until then it has no
# effect and causes no harm.
https://www.texasmovement.com/* https://texasmovement.com/:splat 301!
